cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "STUR Physics Lab: one simulation (production v2.2)"
abstract: >-
  One self-contained Python simulation (standard library only) with nothing
  tuned and nothing fitted. Part A computes flat Lambda-CDM cosmology from
  measured inputs: the radiation density from the CMB temperature, the dark
  energy density from flatness, and the age of the universe. Part B runs the
  measured quark masses with the renormalization group, builds the Fritzsch
  six-zero texture exactly, and scans its two free phases over their full
  range. It finds |V_cb| outside the predicted band for every phase.
authors:
